    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** offense features three standout starts today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27), who both benefit significantly from favorable matchups against high-xERA arms. **Gunnar Henderson** is our premier play, capitalizing on a stellar park factor and a soft SP matchup against Rea; despite a slight hit for holding back on SB attempts, his elite spot at the top of the order makes him a must-start. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** draws a favorable 5.01 xERA assignment against Cabrera, bolstered by a strong platoon advantage that pushes his efficiency well into the elite tier. **Kyle Tucker** (75.04) remains a force to be reckoned with, as the matchup against Hughes offers a prime opportunity for power production that outweighs his mid-order slotting. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Curtis Mead** (61.43) are not in the top-tier of raw output, they are both highly recommended starts today against Arrighetti, benefiting from a combination of park effects and strong platoon positioning.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench today involved **Brayan Rocchio**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 51.40 score. While **Brayan Rocchio** provides respectable value, he lacks the situational ceiling of **Miguel Vargas** (53.76), whose elite xwOBA and stolen base potential against Bennett ultimately secured his inclusion in the 3B slot. We are exercising caution with **Heliot Ramos** (43.02) and **Josh Lowe** (41.60) today; both are on the lower end of our starting threshold. **Heliot Ramos** faces a formidable hurdle in Cease (2.97 xERA), and **Josh Lowe** is hit hard by a negative platoon shift, though his speed profile keeps him active. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains sidelined on the IL. As always, keep an eye on the official lineups for **Liam Hicks**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Sam Antonacci** to ensure no late-breaking weather or managerial changes disrupt our calculated efficiency.",
